# Journal AI - Project Structure

This is an AI-powered mental health journaling platform with a React frontend, Express backend, PostgreSQL database, and Ollama AI integration.

## Project Layout

- **Backend**: [backend/server.js](mdc:backend/server.js) - Express.js API server
- **Frontend**: [frontend/src/index.js](mdc:frontend/src/index.js) - React application entry point
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with schema defined in [backend/server.js](mdc:backend/server.js)
- **Containerization**: [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Multi-container setup

## Key Technologies

### Backend
- Express.js REST API
- PostgreSQL database (pg driver)
- Ollama AI integration for journal analysis
- CORS enabled for frontend communication
- Environment variables via dotenv

### Frontend
- React 18 with functional components and hooks
- Speech recognition API for voice input
- Axios for API calls
- Responsive design with gradient styling

### AI Integration
- Ollama server running locally (default: localhost:11434)
- AI endpoints for analysis and chat
- Model: llama2

## Database Schema

Table: `journal_entries`
- id (SERIAL PRIMARY KEY)
- title (VARCHAR(255))
- content (TEXT NOT NULL)
- ai_response (TEXT)
- created_at (TIMESTAMP)
- updated_at (TIMESTAMP)

## Development

- Backend runs on port 5000
- Frontend runs on port 3000
- Database runs on port 5432
- Use `docker-compose up` to start all services
